      <text id="572:1969" name="Mini App States document the primary interface scenarios within the Telegram Mini App to ensure consistent behavior across different devices, operating systems, and system interactions. These states define how the layout should adapt when the system keyboard appears, bottom sheets are displayed, or the available viewport changes. During keyboard interactions, the interface should automatically adjust by keeping the focused input visible, allowing content to scroll, hiding temporary UI elements such as the bottom navigation, removing the bottom safe area, and ensuring that interactive components remain accessible without being obscured. This documentation serves as the reference for implementing responsive layout behavior and maintaining a consistent user experience throughout the application." x="44" y="104" width="936" height="256" />
    </frame>
